.Dd November 15, 2026
.Dt EMMC2 8
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm emmc2
.Nd Raspberry Pi 4 EMMC2 SD host driver
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm /sbin/emmc2
.Op Ar test
.Op Ar mmio_handle Ns = Ns Ar n
.Op Ar dma_handle Ns = Ns Ar n
.Op Ar irq_handle Ns = Ns Ar n
.Op Ar mmio_size Ns = Ns Ar bytes
.Op Ar dma_size Ns = Ns Ar bytes
.Op Ar clock Ns = Ns Ar hz
.Op Ar window_bus Ns = Ns Ar address
.Op Ar window_cpu Ns = Ns Ar address
.Op Ar window_size Ns = Ns Ar bytes
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
initialises the BCM2711 EMMC2 SDHCI controller and serves the
.Dq disk:
scheme with the
.Xr blockd 8
framing.  It resets the controller, applies 3.3 V, runs the SD
identification sequence at 400 kHz, selects the 25 MHz default clock and the
four-bit bus, and then programs SDMA transfers on the mapped DMA buffer.
.Pp
In real mode the launcher passes the MMIO, DMA and interrupt handles and the
DMA window and clock values.  The defaults are handles 3/4/5, a 256-byte
register window, a 64 KiB DMA buffer, and the Pi 4
.Pa emmc2bus
window bus
.Li 0xc0000000 ,
CPU
.Li 0 ,
size 1 GiB.  A buffer whose bus address does not fit the window is refused with
.Er EIO
rather than truncated.  The command, transfer, ADMA/DMA and timeout errors are
mapped from the SDHCI status registers.
.Pp
The driver serves INFO, READ, WRITE and FLUSH on path
.Dq 0 ;
LIST returns
.Er EINVAL
because partition discovery belongs to
.Xr blockd 8 .
.Pp
With
.Ar test
the driver uses a host-backed memory disk instead of MMIO: it writes a
sector-stamped pattern and an FNV-1a checksum marker, serves
.Dq disk: ,
and exits after a client flush.  This is the mode used by the
.Ql pi4-emmc2
qtest.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /etc/services.d/emmc2.toml -compact
.It Pa /etc/services.d/emmc2.toml
service manifest used by
.Xr init 8
on a platform image
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr blockd 8 ,
.Xr devd 8 ,
.Xr platd 8
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
driver first appeared in RavenBSD 0.1.
.Sh CAVEATS
The real MMIO, interrupt and SDMA path is UNVERIFIED until a Pi 4 board log
exists.  The current data path uses SDMA; ADMA2 is modelled and tested but not
selected by the driver.
